"How do I transfer ownership of my Household? – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-150/articles/29206380198162-How-do-I-transfer-ownership-of-my-Household)\nciteturn783search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; For detailed steps on this process, check out our support article here: How do I delete my Household? ... Once you click 'Leave this household', a window will appear where you can choose to either specify another member as the new owner of the Household or dissolve (delete) the Household entirely.\n\n# How do I transfer ownership of my Household?\n\nIf you have already set up a Toniebox in your Household but would like to give the Toniebox as a gift, you will need to transfer ownership of the Household to the gift recipient.\n\nTo transfer ownership of your Household, you will first need to invite the other member into your Household. For a walkthrough on this process, check out our support article here: How do I invite other members into my Household?\n\nIt is also important to note that, in order to transfer ownership of a Household to another member, that member must not already be the owner of their own Household. If they have already set up their own Household and do not own a Toniebox, they will need to delete their Household. For detailed steps on this process, check out our support article here: How do I delete my Household?\n\nOnce these steps have been completed, you are ready to transfer ownership of your Household! To do this, follow these steps:\n\n  1. Login to your account at my.tonies.com and click the 'Members' tab.\nImage: TransferStep1.jpg\n \n  2. Click the 'Household preferences' dropdown.\nImage: TransferStep2.jpg\n \n  3. Click 'Leave this household'.\nImage: TransferStep3.jpg\n \n  4. Once you click 'Leave this household', a window will appear where you can choose to either specify another member as the new owner of the Household or dissolve (delete) the Household entirely. Choose the intended new owner of the Household by clicking the white circle next to their name and email address. It's important to note that you will not see a recipient listed here if they already own their own Household.\nImage: TransferStep4.jpg\n \n  5. Once you have specified the intended new owner, click 'Set New Owner'.\nImage: TransferStep5.jpg\n \n  6. This will transfer ownership of the Household to the new member and you will automatically leave the Household. If you would like to rejoin the Household, the new owner will simply need to invite you back into the Household with the same process you used before to invite them.\n \n\nIf you are having any trouble transferring ownership of your Household, send us a message and we will help guide you through the process!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow do I delete my Household? – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-au/articles/29036630818578-How-do-I-delete-my-Household)\nciteturn783search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; # How do I delete my Household? ... Click on 'Delete this household'. ... If you are having any trouble deleting your Household, send us a message and we will help guide you through the process!\n\n# How do I delete my Household?\n\nIf you need to delete your Household for any reason, it's important to know that this process will also permanently delete all data, including any recordings that are on Creative Tonies in your Household. If you would like to proceed with deleting your Household, follow the steps below.\n\nHow to delete your Household:\n\nUsing the tonies app\n\n  1. Open the tonies app and tap your profile picture in the top-right side of the screen.\nImage: Profile__1_.jpg\n \n  2. Tap 'Household'.\nImage: Permissions_Step_2.jpg\n \n  3. Tap the settings icon in the upper-right hand side of the screen.\nImage: Delete_HH_Step_3.jpg\n \n  4. Tap 'Dissolve Household'.\nImage: Delete_HH_Step_4.jpg\n \n  5. Tap the red 'Delete' button to confirm that you wish to permanently delete the Household.\nImage: DeleteHH__2_.jpg\n \n  6. You have now successfully deleted your Household and all data will also be permanently deleted.\n\nUsing my.tonies.com\n\n  1. Login to your account at my.tonies.com and click the 'Members' tab.\nImage: TransferStep1.jpg\n \n  2. Click the 'Household preferences' dropdown.\nImage: Step2Delete.jpg\n \n  3. Click on 'Delete this household'.\nImage: Step3Delete.jpg\n \n  4. Click on 'Delete Household' in the window that appears to confirm that you wish to permanently delete the Household.\nImage: Step4Delete.jpg\n \n  5. You have now successfully deleted your Household and all data will also be permanently deleted.\n\nIf you are having any trouble deleting your Household, send us a message and we will help guide you through the process!--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow do I start a return? – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-gb/articles/29036546250642-How-do-I-start-a-return)\nciteturn783search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Make sure to follow through the processes listed in the articles below to reset the Toniebox to factory settings and choose to either delete your Household or just remove the Toniebox from your Household before initiating your return: ...   * How do I delete my Household?\n\n# How do I start a return?\n\nHow to return? \nTo start your return, please visit our returns portal here:\nhttps://app.claimlane.com/c/tonies-uk-rma?lang=en\nSimply enter your order number and the email address used for your purchase to verify your order. Then, select the items you’d like to return.\nOnce you’ve submitted your return, you’ll receive a confirmation email with your shipping label. No need to print at home - just show the QR code from your email to the Post Office and they’ll print your label for you.\nPlease also consider that the items that you would like to return are in complete, unused and undamaged condition per our returns policy: What is your return policy?\nTo start a return from Ireland, please contact our tonies® Support Team via contact form.\nKindly note that we do not offer exchanges. \n\nWhat happens next?\n\n \n\nAfter your return has arrived at our warehouse, we will refund the purchase amount to your chosen payment method within 4 weeks of the arrival date. Please note that you will not receive an automatic confirmation of the receipt of your return, you will however be informed via email once your refund has been processed. \nReturning a Toniebox? \n\n \n\nMake sure to follow through the processes listed in the articles below to reset the Toniebox to factory settings and choose to either delete your Household or just remove the Toniebox from your Household before initiating your return:\n\n  * How do I reset the Toniebox 1 to factory settings?\n  * How do I delete my Household?\n  * How do I remove a Toniebox from my Household?--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAccount – tonies® Support (https://support.tonies.com/hc/en-150/sections/29036387798930-Account)\nciteturn783search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; ### How do I transfer ownership of my Household?\n\n# Account\n\n### Popular Articles\n\nAccount\n\n### Topics\n\nManaging Your Household Customisation All Other Articles\n\n## Managing Your Household\n\n5 articles\n\n### How do I transfer ownership of my Household?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### How to create a my.tonies account\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### How do I invite other members into my Household?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### How do I manage Household members permissions?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n### How do I change the name of my Household?\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n## Customisation\n\n1 articles\n\n### Change your personal data\n\nRead Full Article →\n\n## All Other Articles\n\n1 articles\n\n### tonies® Account - Google Sign In\n\nRead Full Article →---------------------------------------